# VoicePulse → Google Sheets Integration

## Step 1 — Create a Google Sheet

1. Open [Google Sheets](https://sheets.google.com) and create a new spreadsheet.
2. Name it `VoicePulse Responses` (or anything you like).
3. Add a header row in **Row 1** with these exact column names:

| A | B | C | D | E | F | G | H | I | J | K | L | M | N | O | P | Q | R |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Timestamp | Session ID | Respondent Name | Context | Q1 | A1 | Q2 | A2 | Q3 | A3 | Q4 | A4 | Q5 | A5 | Summary | Avg Sentiment | Themes | Actions | Hindsight Corrections |

> [!TIP]
> You can skip the headers — the script appends data regardless. Headers just make it readable.

---

## Step 2 — Create the Apps Script

1. In your Google Sheet, click **Extensions → Apps Script**
2. Delete any existing code and paste the following:

```javascript
// VoicePulse Google Sheets Recorder
// Receives POST from the VoicePulse frontend and appends a row to Sheet1.

function doPost(e) {
  try {
    var sheet = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet().getSheets()[0];
    var data = JSON.parse(e.postData.contents);

    sheet.appendRow([
      data.timestamp          || "",
      data.sessionId          || "",
      data.respondentName     || "",
      data.context            || "",
      data.q1 || "",  data.a1 || "",
      data.q2 || "",  data.a2 || "",
      data.q3 || "",  data.a3 || "",
      data.q4 || "",  data.a4 || "",
      data.q5 || "",  data.a5 || "",
      data.summary            || "",
      data.avgSentiment       || 0,
      data.themes             || "",
      data.actions            || "",
      data.hindsightCorrections || 0
    ]);

    return ContentService
      .createTextOutput(JSON.stringify({ status: "ok" }))
      .setMimeType(ContentService.MimeType.JSON);

  } catch (err) {
    return ContentService
      .createTextOutput(JSON.stringify({ status: "error", message: err.toString() }))
      .setMimeType(ContentService.MimeType.JSON);
  }
}

// Optional: test via GET (visit URL in browser to verify deployment)
// Updated to return all sheet data as JSON for the Analyser
function doGet(e) {
  try {
    var sheet = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet().getSheets()[0];
    var data = sheet.getDataRange().getValues();
    var headers = data[0];
    var rows = data.slice(1);
    
    var jsonData = rows.map(function(row) {
      var obj = {};
      headers.forEach(function(header, i) {
        obj[header] = row[i];
      });
      return obj;
    });

    return ContentService
      .createTextOutput(JSON.stringify(jsonData))
      .setMimeType(ContentService.MimeType.JSON);
  } catch (err) {
    return ContentService
      .createTextOutput(JSON.stringify({ status: "error", message: err.toString() }))
      .setMimeType(ContentService.MimeType.JSON);
  }
}
```

---

## Step 3 — Deploy as Web App

1. Click **Deploy → New Deployment**
2. Click the ⚙️ gear icon → Select type: **Web App**
3. Configure:
   - **Description**: `VoicePulse Recorder`
   - **Execute as**: `Me`
   - **Who has access**: `Anyone` *(required for frontend to POST without auth)*
4. Click **Deploy**
5. Authorize the permissions when prompted (Allow → Google Account)
6. **Copy the Web App URL** — it looks like:
   ```
   https://script.google.com/macros/s/AKfycbx.../exec
   ```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Every time you edit the Apps Script code, you must create a **New Deployment** (not update existing) for changes to take effect.

---

## Step 4 — Connect to VoicePulse

1. Open VoicePulse in your browser
2. Navigate to **Operator Console → MANAGE_API_KEYS**
3. Paste the Apps Script URL into the **Google Sheets Apps Script URL** field
4. Click **SAVE_SETTINGS**

The header badge will immediately change from `SHEETS_OFF` to `SHEETS_CONNECTED` ✅.

---

## What Gets Recorded Per Session

Every completed VoicePulse feedback session automatically appends **one row** with:

| Column | Content |
|--------|---------|
| Timestamp | ISO 8601 timestamp of session completion |
| Session ID | Unique `session_<unix>` identifier |
| Respondent Name | Auto-assigned (e.g. `Respondent #3`) |
| Context | Campaign context string |
| Q1–Q5 / A1–A5 | Each interviewer question and respondent answer (up to 5 turns) |
| Summary | AI executive summary of the session |
| Avg Sentiment | 0–100 composite sentiment score |
| Themes | Semicolon-separated theme list with sentiment labels |
| Actions | Semicolon-separated operator action items with priority |
| Hindsight Corrections | Count of retrospective tag corrections |

> [!NOTE]
> The frontend uses `mode: "no-cors"` for the POST request, which means network responses are opaque. A successful network send is treated as success — check the Sheet itself to verify rows are appearing.
